# Millennium backup config — copy to infra/hetzner/backup.env (chmod 600), read
# by millennium-backup.service as an EnvironmentFile. Kept SEPARATE from any
# co-tenant's crontab env on purpose: Millennium must use its OWN R2 bucket + OWN
# scoped rclone remote, never another app's. backup.env is gitignored.

# Where local dumps land (default: $HOME/millennium-backups). Keep it outside the repo.
# BACKUP_DIR=/home/millennium/millennium-backups

# How many most-recent LOCAL dumps to retain (default 7).
# KEEP=7

# Off-box mirror — effectively REQUIRED: the backup script FAILS CLOSED if this is
# unset (a backup that only lives on the VPS dies with it). Millennium's OWN rclone
# remote, scoped to a Millennium-only bucket; configure it under the millennium
# user (`rclone config` → ~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf, no_check_bucket=true).
# Uncomment + set it:
# BACKUP_REMOTE=r2-millennium:millennium-db-backups

# Escape hatch — set to 1 to run LOCAL-ONLY backups (e.g. before R2 is wired up).
# Then the success ping means a local dump only; the VPS-loss risk is yours.
# ALLOW_LOCAL_ONLY_BACKUP=1

# Off-box retention in days (default 30).
# OFFSITE_KEEP_DAYS=30

# Optional healthchecks.io-style dead-man's-switch URL (its own, not shared).
# BACKUP_HEALTHCHECK_URL=https://hc-ping.com/your-millennium-uuid
